+# Implementation Plan: Multi-attempt Solving with Reproducible Test Harness
+
+## Constraints Analysis
+- The system must support reproducible testing with seed/mode parameters for `gen.py`
+- Must handle multiple candidates (solutions) and objectively evaluate them
+- Must implement a bounded workflow (K=3 attempts, MAX_ROUNDS=2 reflection rounds)
+- Must NOT use `while True` loops anywhere
+- Tools must have valid JSON schemas with proper nesting (required at same level as properties, every property has type and description)
+
+## Implementation Tasks
+
+### 1. New Tool: `tools/evaluate_candidates.py`
+**Schema Requirements:**
+- Properties: solution_paths (array of strings), brute_path (string), generator_path (string), checker_path (optional string), num_seeds (integer), timeout_sec (number), samples_dir (string), max_input_path (optional string)
+- Required: [solution_paths, brute_path, generator_path, num_seeds, timeout_sec, samples_dir]
+
+**Behavior:**
+- For each candidate: run all sample files in samples_dir/*.in against *.out
+- Generate test cases: for seed in range(num_seeds), for mode in [tiny, random, edge, max]
+  - Call `python3 gen.py <seed> <mode>`
+  - Run brute force (skip for max mode - timing only)
+  - Run each candidate
+  - Compare via checker (argv: input_file expected_file actual_file) or exact match
+- Track: timeouts, runtime errors as failures
+- Save first failing input to fail_input.txt next to candidate
+- Report: sample passes, per-mode random pass counts, max-input runtime, pairwise disagreements, final ranking with best candidate path
+
+### 2. Update `tools/run_tests.py`
+- Call generator with `<seed> <mode>` arguments
+- Use argv-based checker interface
+- Save failing inputs to disk
+- Keep schema valid
+
+### 3. Refactor `coding_agent.py`
+**New Methods:**
+- `build_tests()`: Create tests_work/brute.py, gen.py with modes, samples/, optional checker.py
+- `solve_attempt(i, hint, prior_feedback)`: K=3 independent attempts, each writing to attempts/attempt_i/solution.py
+- `evaluate_candidates()`: Call the new tool, capture report
+- `reflect_round(round_idx, report)`: Up to MAX_ROUNDS=2, give best code + failing inputs to agent for diagnosis
+- `finalize(best_path)`: Copy best to target, delete scratch files (tests_work/, attempts/), re-run samples
+
+**Constants:** K=3, MAX_ROUNDS=2
+**Loop Structure:** Only use bounded `for` loops, never `while True`
+**Early Exit:** When a candidate passes everything and no disagreement with others
+
+## Key Implementation Details
+
+1. **Generator Interface:**
+   - Old: `python3 gen.py` -> stdout test case
+   - New: `python3 gen.py <seed> <mode>` -> stdout test case for reproducible, mode-specific generation
+   - Modes: tiny (minimal), random (random values), edge (boundary cases), max (worst-case timing)
+
+2. **Checker Interface:**
+   - Argv-based: `python3 checker.py <input_file> <expected_file> <actual_file>`
+   - Exit code 0 = pass, non-zero = fail
+   - Alternative: exact match with token-wise whitespace-insensitive comparison
+
+3. **Candidate Ranking:**
+   - Samples weight highest (pass/fail on provided samples)
+   - Then random passes (number of modes that pass)
+   - Then max-input success
+   - Then speed
+
+4. **Failure Tracking:**
+   - Each failing candidate gets a fail_input.txt with:
+     - First failing input (truncated if large)
+     - Expected output
+     - Actual output
+     - Timing information
+
+5. **Feedback Accumulation:**
+   - Solve attempts receive prior failure summaries
+   - Reflection rounds receive concrete failing inputs with expected/actual output
+
+## Files to Create/Modify
+- [ ] Create: `/dgm/tools/evaluate_candidates.py`
+- [ ] Modify: `/dgm/tools/run_tests.py` (add seed/mode parameters)
+- [ ] Modify: `/dgm/coding_agent.py` (add helper methods, refactor forward())
